            <bibl xml:id="bibl_12"><title key="work_7859">Vitas patrum.
                                                Collections with this common title invariably begin
                                                with Rufinus's translation (often ascribed to
                                                Jerome) of the Historia monachorum in Aegypto (PL
                                                21. 387—462; ed. E. Schulz-Flügel [Berlin 1990]),
                                                and then go on to include other Lives and
                                                apophthegmata of the type collected and published by
                                                H. Rosweyde and reprinted in PL vols. 73—4. Jerome's
                                                Lives of St Paul the Hermit, St Hilarion, and St
                                                Malchus (CPL 617—19) also make a frequent
